WHAT THIS ADDS
  A public, read-only GET /api/servers on the bot, so the website's new Servers page
  (https://spinback-j7ao5f.camelai.app/servers.html) can list every Rust server the bot
  looks after: whatever the bot has measured, with the population, map and last check
  whenever the bot knows them.

  The page reads /api/servers first and falls back to the public /api/status, so nothing
  breaks while this is unapplied - it just reports the one server the public status
  carries, and says so on the page.

WHERE
  bot/server.mjs, in the HTTP request handler, directly AFTER the existing
  'GET /api/guilds' block. The route stays public and above the settings-auth gate: it
  is read-only and publishes nothing private (no password, no address, no tokens).

CONTRACT THE PAGE EXPECTS
  Missing fields are printed as "not reported", never guessed, so you may leave any of
  players / maxPlayers / map / ms out until the bot knows them.

  { "ok": true, "count": 1, "servers": [ {
      "id": "srv_1",
      "name": "Spinback 5X EU",
      "guild": "Spinback",
      "online": true,
      "players": 42,
      "maxPlayers": 100,
      "map": "Procedural Map",
      "ms": 38,
      "checkedAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
      "reason": null,
      "detail": "already address-stripped, or null"
  } ] }

  host and port are deliberately not sent: the bot's own status strips addresses, so the
  page prints "Address not reported". To publish them, add host/port to the object below
  and nothing else on the site has to change.

STEP 1 - the minimal version: something the bot has already measured, no new connections
------------------------------------------------------------------------------- cut here
  /* Every Rust server the bot looks after, for the website's Servers page. Public and
     read-only on purpose: nothing here is not already reported to a browser by
     /api/status, and the address and password stay in the bot. */
  let serversCache = { at: 0, body: null };
  if (req.method === 'GET' && url === '/api/servers') {
    const cors = { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'public, max-age=30',
      'access-control-allow-origin': '*' };
    if (!serversCache.body || Date.now() - serversCache.at > 30000) {
      const list = (settings.servers || []).map(function (server) {
        const check = serverChecks[server.id] || null;
        return {
          id: server.id,
          name: server.name || 'Rust server',
          guild: (state.guildInfo && state.guildInfo.name) || null,
          online: !!(check && check.ok),
          state: check ? (check.ok ? 'online' : 'offline') : 'unknown',
          ms: check && typeof check.ms === 'number' ? check.ms : null,
          checkedAt: check ? check.at : null,
          reason: check && !check.ok ? (check.reason || 'unknown') : null,
          detail: null,
        };
      });
      serversCache = { at: Date.now(), body: JSON.stringify({ ok: true, count: list.length, servers: list }) };
    }
    res.writeHead(200, cors);
    res.end(serversCache.body);
    return;
  }
